1
00:00:04,563 --> 00:00:05,916
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۞

2
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:08,090
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۞

3
00:00:08,488 --> 00:00:10,324
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:12,207 --> 00:00:19,135
The time preceding the Prophethood, of Muhammadﷺ was a time of darkness.

5
00:00:20,516 --> 00:00:24,603
However, there were some glimpses of light here and there,

6
00:00:25,687 --> 00:00:29,727
but they were too few and far, in between.

7
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:37,142
And humanity was in dire need of Hidayah(هداية), guidance.

8
00:00:37,801 --> 00:00:47,424
But again, there were some individuals here and there, scattered apart, who had the sense of right and wrong,

9
00:00:48,364 --> 00:00:52,777
and their hearts directed them to the truth.

10
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:55,770
And we'll talk about a few of these examples.

11
00:00:56,348 --> 00:01:00,753
One of them is; Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل).

12
00:01:01,722 --> 00:01:05,102
Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) went out in search of truth,

13
00:01:05,189 --> 00:01:09,371
he traveled out of Makkah searching for the truth, he was from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

14
00:01:10,095 --> 00:01:14,079
but he traveled around in search of guidance.

15
00:01:16,079 --> 00:01:23,421
So, he went to the Jews, and inquired about their religion, but he decided not to follow it.

16
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:30,711
And then he went to the Christians and inquired about their religion, and decided not to follow it.

17
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:44,560
And then in the end, he came to learn about the way of Ibrahim عليه السّلام; Al-Hanifiya(الحنفيه), worshipping Allah alone.

18
00:01:45,587 --> 00:01:53,311
And he became a Haneefi(حنيفي); a follower of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

19
00:01:54,492 --> 00:02:00,532
Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) was a lone voice in the sea of darkness in Makkah.

20
00:02:01,797 --> 00:02:11,376
Asmaa Bint Abi Bakr(اسماء بنت ابي بكر); she said that I have seen Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) with his back leaning on Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

21
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:17,738
And he's speaking to his people, of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and telling them: O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

22
00:02:18,198 --> 00:02:22,944
none of you is following the way of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) except myself.

23
00:02:23,948 --> 00:02:28,137
Because the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) use to claim that they are the inheritors of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

24
00:02:28,217 --> 00:02:29,970
they are the ones following his path.

25
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:38,543
But Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) would tell them none of you is following the true path of Ibrahim عليه السّلام, other than me.

26
00:02:38,988 --> 00:02:41,328
Asmaa(اسماء), the daughter of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said:

27
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:46,840
I saw Zaid Bin Amr Bin Nufail(زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل), leaning his back against the Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) saying;

28
00:02:47,222 --> 00:02:51,436
O tribe of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) by Him in Whose hand is Zaid(زيد) soul,

29
00:02:51,817 --> 00:02:56,809
not one of you apart from myself follows the religion of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

30
00:02:57,396 --> 00:03:05,389
He would also say O God if only I knew the way most favored by you, I would worship you by it,

31
00:03:05,697 --> 00:03:06,546
But I don't know.

32
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:11,659
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), he believes in Allah, he knows the truth,

33
00:03:12,134 --> 00:03:15,847
but he doesn't know how to apply it how to worship Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

34
00:03:15,887 --> 00:03:17,517
he doesn't have Shariah(شريعه) to follow.

35
00:03:17,912 --> 00:03:22,226
He has the belief, he has the faith and he wants to pray to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, but he doesn't know, how?

36
00:03:22,674 --> 00:03:26,626
And there are people like Zaid(زيد) in every time

37
00:03:27,476 --> 00:03:32,128
people whose hearts guide them to the truth, they know that there's no god but one,

38
00:03:32,619 --> 00:03:35,143
and they want to worship Allahسبحانه وتعالى

39
00:03:35,391 --> 00:03:38,356
but they haven't been exposed to the way to do it.

40
00:03:39,151 --> 00:03:43,583
And in fact, some reverts have been through such an experience.

41
00:03:43,845 --> 00:03:49,903
 I know, of one brother who later on became a Muslim, he became Muslim at the age of 40.

42
00:03:50,357 --> 00:03:57,967
He used to say that in my heart, I knew that Allah is one and Allah had no son,

43
00:03:58,468 --> 00:04:03,627
and I would not drink and I would not eat pork because I thought that these are not good.

44
00:04:03,999 --> 00:04:08,846
And I would avoid the sins that people would participate in I felt that in my heart

45
00:04:10,198 --> 00:04:13,517
and I wanted to pray to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, but I would not know how?

46
00:04:14,351 --> 00:04:15,978
Until I learned about Islam(The Religion Of Ibrahim عليه السّلام).

47
00:04:16,706 --> 00:04:20,165
So, here you have Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) going though the same experience,

48
00:04:20,651 --> 00:04:24,467
he is saying O Allah I want to pray to you, but I don't know how.

49
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:28,211
And we'll talk about Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), who has some similar words.

50
00:04:29,466 --> 00:04:35,304
It's amazing to see Ya'ani(يعني) how many things Zaid(زيد) knew by his natural disposition.

51
00:04:37,452 --> 00:04:43,102
For example, He would not participate in the killing of girls that existed in Makkah.

52
00:04:43,928 --> 00:04:49,087
In fact whenever he hears about father about to kill his daughter,

53
00:04:49,451 --> 00:04:53,614
he would go to that father and say Give her to me, I'll take care of her!

54
00:04:55,228 --> 00:04:58,376
So, he would adopt all of these girls and raise them up.

55
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:04,116
It says here, he would give life back to girls about to be killed at birth,

56
00:05:04,507 --> 00:05:06,646
telling a man wishing to kill his daughter.

57
00:05:06,885 --> 00:05:07,977
Don't kill her.

58
00:05:08,163 --> 00:05:10,060
Give her to me to look after.

59
00:05:10,514 --> 00:05:15,826
When she grows up, you can take her back or if you wish, Give her to me.

60
00:05:16,508 --> 00:05:18,300
So, he would raise up these daughters,

61
00:05:18,525 --> 00:05:21,771
and then go back to the father and say if you want her back,

62
00:05:22,079 --> 00:05:25,211
here she is otherwise, I would still take care of her.

63
00:05:26,158 --> 00:05:30,672
He used to refuse to eat the meat that was slaughtered in Makkah.

64
00:05:31,926 --> 00:05:35,300
It's mentioned that once a meal was presented to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

65
00:05:35,806 --> 00:05:36,688
some meat,

66
00:05:36,974 --> 00:05:40,990
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused it and he passed it over,

67
00:05:41,450 --> 00:05:44,116
so it was given to Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل),

68
00:05:44,283 --> 00:05:48,233
Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) said I don't eat from this meat which you slaughter for your gods.

69
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:52,713
He used to, in fact there's a quotation by him;

70
00:05:53,888 --> 00:05:55,614
He would go to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

71
00:05:56,012 --> 00:06:01,257
and he would criticize them for slaughtering their beasts in the names of their gods.

72
00:06:01,492 --> 00:06:04,001
He would say, "sheep were created by God,

73
00:06:04,541 --> 00:06:10,597
and He brings down from the skies, the water that makes vegetation, grow for them from the earth.

74
00:06:11,033 --> 00:06:14,616
So, why do you slaughter them in the name of God other than Allah,

75
00:06:14,808 --> 00:06:17,780
denying all that and venerating them.

76
00:06:18,119 --> 00:06:21,593
He said, Allah is the One, Who created these cattle and you know that

77
00:06:21,817 --> 00:06:24,176
and Allah is the One, Who's bringing down rain for them,

78
00:06:24,581 --> 00:06:27,485
and then you are slaughtering them in the name of other gods.

79
00:06:29,082 --> 00:06:36,801
Now Zaid Bin Amr Bin Nufail(زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل), he died prior to the Prophet hood of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

80
00:06:37,315 --> 00:06:40,496
His son Saeed(سعيد) was one of the believers

81
00:06:42,327 --> 00:06:46,269
and he is one of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة), Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد).

82
00:06:47,736 --> 00:06:51,042
Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and inquired about his father,

83
00:06:51,257 --> 00:06:54,500
he wanted to know what will be the fate of his father?

84
00:06:55,721 --> 00:06:57,731
Because he died before Prophet Hood.

85
00:06:57,966 --> 00:07:07,492
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told Saeed(سعيد) that your father will come on the day of judgment as a nation alone.

86
00:07:08,682 --> 00:07:15,095
Rasool Allah ﷺ has given Zaid Bin Amr(زيد بن عمرو) glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

87
00:07:16,488 --> 00:07:23,764
And he also mentioned that on the Day of Judgment, Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل) will be standing as a nation by himself.

88
00:07:24,512 --> 00:07:28,804
On the day of judgment people are going to be divided into nations

89
00:07:29,201 --> 00:07:31,038
and every nation is led by a Prophet.

90
00:07:32,123 --> 00:07:33,729
So, you'd have the nation of Noah(نوح),

91
00:07:34,207 --> 00:07:39,265
the nation of Musa(موسى),  the nation of Eesa(عيسى), the nation of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

92
00:07:39,659 --> 00:07:41,913
And you would have the nation of Muhammadﷺ

93
00:07:42,855 --> 00:07:49,259
because Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل), was not part of a particular nation of a Prophet,

94
00:07:49,585 --> 00:07:52,853
he would come on the day of judgment as his own nation,

95
00:07:53,384 --> 00:07:55,345
he would be standing alone.

96
00:07:56,458 --> 00:08:02,365
And that is also an honor for Zaid Bin Nufail(زيد بن نفيل), that he is standing on the Day of Judgment alone

97
00:08:02,674 --> 00:08:06,013
 And Allah سبحانه وتعالى will grant him Jannah(جنة),

98
00:08:06,574 --> 00:08:10,254
 because he knew the truth and he worshiped Allahسبحانه وتعالى the best he could.

99
00:08:11,734 --> 00:08:13,728
Another example is Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل).

100
00:08:14,641 --> 00:08:20,735
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) was the cousin of Khadijah رضي الله عنها.

101
00:08:21,189 --> 00:08:23,442
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل), was a Christian.

102
00:08:24,292 --> 00:08:26,775
And he was a lettered man

103
00:08:27,251 --> 00:08:32,258
and he used to copy some of the Scripture of the Christians and study from it

104
00:08:32,672 --> 00:08:34,854
and he had some of these scrolls.

105
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:39,666
And he was a believer in one God, he was a believer in Allahعَزّوجَلّ

106
00:08:40,147 --> 00:08:43,123
and again, there were some Christians here and there

107
00:08:43,148 --> 00:08:46,051
who still believed in the oneness of Allah سبحانه وتعالى

108
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:49,514
and they would not attribute divinity to Eesa عليه السّلام.

109
00:08:49,689 --> 00:08:51,530
Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) was one of them.

110
00:08:51,858 --> 00:08:54,719
And Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) was the one, Khadijah(خديجه) consulted,

111
00:08:55,022 --> 00:08:57,426
When Rasool Allah ﷺ first received the revelation.

112
00:08:57,942 --> 00:09:00,354
Immediately after that, Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) passed away.

113
00:09:00,672 --> 00:09:03,512
So, people were wondering what would happen to Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل).

114
00:09:04,082 --> 00:09:06,770
And some of them were saying Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) is in Hellfire

115
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:11,419
because he died before Rasool Allah ﷺ started preaching the message,

116
00:09:11,711 --> 00:09:16,370
even though Rasool Allah had received the message, but he didn't start preaching it yet.

117
00:09:17,058 --> 00:09:19,343
And Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) died before that.

118
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,486
So, they said that he would be in Hellfire.

119
00:09:21,734 --> 00:09:27,884
Rasool Allah ﷺ said I have seen him in a dream and he was wearing white clothes,

120
00:09:28,524 --> 00:09:34,470
if he was a man in Hellfire, he wouldn't be wearing white clothes.

121
00:09:36,025 --> 00:09:38,838
Later on, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw another dream

122
00:09:39,602 --> 00:09:44,328
and Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) had two gardens in paradise.

123
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:50,928
So, he was in Jannah(جنة) because he had the true belief, he had the right belief.

124
00:09:52,182 --> 00:09:56,178
Now the next example is a long one,

125
00:09:56,750 --> 00:10:02,672
it is the story of Salman Al-Farisi رضي الله عنه.

126
00:10:04,339 --> 00:10:11,407
Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه, he went to Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) when he was old, in his old age

127
00:10:12,429 --> 00:10:16,202
and he requested Salman(سلمان) to tell him his story.

128
00:10:17,248 --> 00:10:21,762
So, Salman(سلمان) is now narrating his story to Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه.

129
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:27,445
He says: I was a Persian man from Asfahan(اسفهان).

130
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:34,765
Asfahan(اسفهان) is in current day Iran from a village called Gee(جي).

131
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:39,770
And my father was the head man of the town or the village

132
00:10:41,472 --> 00:10:50,649
and I was striving and taking pain in the religion of Al-Majoosiah(ألمجوسيه).

133
00:10:51,947 --> 00:10:54,728
Al-Majoosiah(ألمجوسيه), I think it's translated as Maggian

134
00:10:55,730 --> 00:11:00,181
it's a religion that they believe in good and evil and they worship fire.

135
00:11:01,446 --> 00:11:04,835
So, they believe that there are two forces that are fighting good and evil.

136
00:11:05,549 --> 00:11:06,921
It's a form of Shirk(شرك),

137
00:11:07,305 --> 00:11:10,531
They are considered to be Wasnia(وثنيه), it's not part of Ahlul Kitaab(أهل الكتاب).

138
00:11:11,236 --> 00:11:15,710
So, Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) says; I took pains to be a good Maggian.

139
00:11:16,626 --> 00:11:20,512
And he grew in the religion, until he became the keeper of the fire.

140
00:11:22,324 --> 00:11:25,982
He was the one who would light the fire and the never let it go off.

141
00:11:27,056 --> 00:11:30,671
So, they had this fire in every village they would have in the temple of fire,

142
00:11:31,212 --> 00:11:36,524
and the fire needs to be kept by a certain person to ensure that it's always burning.

143
00:11:37,663 --> 00:11:45,369
And that was supposed to be a high position in their religion, to be the keeper of the fire, the one who was entrusted with the fire.

144
00:11:45,847 --> 00:11:48,752
He said, my father owned a large farm,

145
00:11:49,290 --> 00:11:53,270
one day he was busy constructing a building of his,

146
00:11:53,771 --> 00:11:58,517
 and he wanted me to go out and take care of business in the farm.

147
00:11:59,346 --> 00:12:02,921
But Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) says that my father loved me so much,

148
00:12:04,089 --> 00:12:08,042
he closeted me in his house and would never let me leave.

149
00:12:09,394 --> 00:12:15,021
So, Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) says on that particular day, my father was busy with this building of his

150
00:12:15,495 --> 00:12:18,772
and he wanted me to go and take care of some business in his farm.

151
00:12:19,669 --> 00:12:22,603
But then he told me, O my son, you know how dear you are to me,

152
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:26,986
if you are late, then I would be so concerned about you and

153
00:12:27,066 --> 00:12:32,127
you are more important to me than the farm or my building, so please come early,

154
00:12:32,759 --> 00:12:34,688
 Salman Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) literally said,

155
00:12:34,957 --> 00:12:40,358
I was kept in his house, like a slave girl, he would not allow me to go anywhere.

156
00:12:41,647 --> 00:12:45,643
Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) he left on that day to go and do this business for his father.

157
00:12:46,395 --> 00:12:52,514
He said, I passed by a church for Christians, it was a Christian church.

158
00:12:53,262 --> 00:12:54,958
And I heard them praying,

159
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:59,589
So, I wanted to go in and investigate and Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) says;

160
00:12:59,851 --> 00:13:03,563
I didn't know much about people because I never left home.

161
00:13:04,293 --> 00:13:06,546
He said: So this was something new to me.

162
00:13:07,414 --> 00:13:12,253
And I came to realize that there's another religion and some people are praying in a different fashion.

163
00:13:12,690 --> 00:13:15,316
So, I decided to go in, and investigate.

164
00:13:15,546 --> 00:13:17,030
He said: I went into the church.

165
00:13:17,715 --> 00:13:21,973
And I was quite impressed by their method of prayer,

166
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,965
I ended up staying with them until sunset.

167
00:13:27,101 --> 00:13:29,485
And I neglected my father's work.

168
00:13:30,258 --> 00:13:32,076
He said: My father was so worried,

169
00:13:32,378 --> 00:13:34,575
he started sending out people to find me.

170
00:13:35,849 --> 00:13:40,630
I came back late and my father said; O, my son, Didn't I tell you not to be late, what happened?

171
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:46,111
Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) said: I passed next to a church of Christians.

172
00:13:46,466 --> 00:13:49,364
And I went in to see their prayer.

173
00:13:50,109 --> 00:13:54,184
And I forgot to do the job you asked me to.

174
00:13:54,849 --> 00:13:58,911
His father told them all my son, their religion is no good,

175
00:13:59,392 --> 00:14:03,241
and your religion, and the religion of your forefathers is better.

176
00:14:05,051 --> 00:14:08,226
Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) responded to his father and said: No

177
00:14:08,613 --> 00:14:10,482
their religion is better than ours.

178
00:14:10,886 --> 00:14:14,679
So, now the father of Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي) was extremely worried.

179
00:14:15,284 --> 00:14:20,774
He ended up chaining, his son and imprisoning him at home.

180
00:14:21,637 --> 00:14:23,281
He put chains on his legs.

181
00:14:23,941 --> 00:14:28,282
He was so terrified and afraid that my son, might change his religion,

182
00:14:28,848 --> 00:14:31,687
that he ended up locking him up at home.

183
00:14:32,748 --> 00:14:36,040
Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان الفارسي), when he was at the church, he asked

184
00:14:36,765 --> 00:14:40,223
the church members, where is the center of your religion?

185
00:14:40,263 --> 00:14:41,975
Where did this religion originate from?

186
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:45,228
So they said from the Holy Land, from Falasteen(فلسطين), from Ash-sham(الشام).

187
00:14:46,012 --> 00:14:52,388
Now, when his father put him in shackles, he managed to send out a message to the church

188
00:14:52,859 --> 00:15:03,747
telling them that if you ever receive or know of a caravan that is in town from Ash-sham(الشام), let me know.

189
