00:30:41,302 --> 00:30:43,753
So, I want to honor you with this gift,

385
00:30:45,127 --> 00:30:48,424
and he said: I handed the food to Muhammadﷺ,

386
00:30:49,292 --> 00:30:55,534
he said: Muhammadﷺ invited the companions to come in, and eat, and he joined with them,

387
00:30:56,574 --> 00:30:57,607
Sign number two.

388
00:30:59,170 --> 00:31:09,150
He said: And then I went to him and visited him, when he was in Baqiyah Al-Gharqad(بقيه ألغرقد), cemetery of Madina.

389
00:31:10,336 --> 00:31:11,786
He was following a Janazah(جنازه).

390
00:31:12,813 --> 00:31:23,731
He said: I went up to Muhammadﷺ I greeted him and then I went around him, to see the sign on his back.

391
00:31:24,589 --> 00:31:27,873
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ sensed

392
00:31:28,298 --> 00:31:31,434
that I was trying to look for something that was described for me.

393
00:31:32,332 --> 00:31:39,733
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered his back he threw off the cloak that was covering his shoulders.

394
00:31:40,667 --> 00:31:46,434
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said, and right there in front of my eyes was the seal of Prophet hood,

395
00:31:47,679 --> 00:31:48,894
Sign number three.

396
00:31:49,329 --> 00:31:54,519
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said when I saw the seal of Prophet hood on his back.

397
00:31:55,297 --> 00:32:03,479
I fell down and I prostrated myself to Muhammadﷺ, I made Sujood(سجود) to him, and I started kissing his feet and I was crying.

398
00:32:04,342 --> 00:32:09,187
And that was the moment that Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي), has been waiting all of his life for.

399
00:32:09,995 --> 00:32:14,897
So, he made Sujood(سجود) to Muhammadﷺ and he was kissing his feet and weeping, crying.

400
00:32:15,740 --> 00:32:18,592
He said: Rasool Allah ﷺ immediately told me to stand up.

401
00:32:19,371 --> 00:32:23,758
Rasool Allah ﷺ does not accept Sujood(سجود) for him.

402
00:32:24,447 --> 00:32:26,076
So, he told Salman(سلمان) to stand up.

403
00:32:26,754 --> 00:32:28,550
And then he told me, tell me your story.

404
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:31,109
So, I narrated my story to him.

405
00:32:31,476 --> 00:32:37,696
Rasool Allah ﷺ told me I want you to narrate, this same story to my companions.

406
00:32:38,035 --> 00:32:40,153
I want you to tell them this story,

407
00:32:40,657 --> 00:32:44,843
a story of a man, who was searching for truth, all of his life.

408
00:32:46,583 --> 00:32:54,439
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: and I narrated my story to them, just like I am narrating it to you, Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس),

409
00:32:54,999 --> 00:32:57,835
I was mentioning to them, the same thing.

410
00:32:59,045 --> 00:33:01,385
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: Because I was a slave,

411
00:33:02,179 --> 00:33:05,872
I ended up missing the Battle of Badr(بدر) and the Battle of Uhud(أحد)

412
00:33:06,726 --> 00:33:11,975
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told me one day, O Salman(سلمان) free yourself from slavery, Kaatib(كاتب).

413
00:33:12,626 --> 00:33:16,951
Mukatiba(مكاتبه) was a deal that was made by the slave and the master,

414
00:33:17,516 --> 00:33:19,769
that the slave would work for a certain time

415
00:33:19,809 --> 00:33:24,311
and generate a certain income and ransom themselves.

416
00:33:24,938 --> 00:33:28,234
So, Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) went to his owner and said: I want to be free.

417
00:33:28,663 --> 00:33:37,186
So, his owner told him, you have to plant for me 300 palm trees and they all have to survive.

418
00:33:37,387 --> 00:33:41,400
 So, at the end, I have to have 300 living palm trees

419
00:33:42,306 --> 00:33:44,525
and you pay me 40 ounces of gold.

420
00:33:45,730 --> 00:33:50,606
So, he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ said: this is the huge amount of money that I have to pay to ransom myself.

421
00:33:51,266 --> 00:33:53,644
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, don't worry.

422
00:33:54,079 --> 00:33:58,665
And then Rasool Ullah gathered the Sahabah and told them, help your brother!

423
00:33:59,633 --> 00:34:04,678
So, Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: Some of them would bring 30 seedlings of a palm tree,

424
00:34:04,732 --> 00:34:09,368
 some of them would bring 20, some 15, everyone would bring as much as they can,

425
00:34:09,972 --> 00:34:12,253
until I had 300 seedlings.

426
00:34:12,881 --> 00:34:17,307
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, when you collect the 300 seedlings

427
00:34:17,635 --> 00:34:22,401
go and dig the holes for them, but do not plant them, come and tell me first.

428
00:34:23,502 --> 00:34:28,825
So, Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) gathered the 300 seedlings, he went and he dug the holes for them.

429
00:34:30,002 --> 00:34:33,084
And then he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said it's already.

430
00:34:33,728 --> 00:34:34,727
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said,

431
00:34:34,767 --> 00:34:44,791
Rasool Allah ﷺ by himself would go and carry the seedlings and plant them one by one with his own blessed hands.

432
00:34:45,542 --> 00:34:53,155
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said, None of those 300 palm trees died, they all grew, they all survived.

433
00:34:54,131 --> 00:35:03,021
Now the ratio of palm trees that end up growing is usually you have a small ratio many of them die, at that young age

434
00:35:03,316 --> 00:35:07,934
because of their fragility and the heat of the desert and the difficult weather.

435
00:35:08,293 --> 00:35:11,901
But Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to do it himself so that they would survive.

436
00:35:12,641 --> 00:35:15,522
So, he planted them one by one and they all lived.

437
00:35:16,312 --> 00:35:20,132
So, now Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) had to pay 40 ounces of gold

438
00:35:20,192 --> 00:35:22,672
and he had no clue where he's going to get that amount of money from.

439
00:35:23,659 --> 00:35:29,529
Later on one day, a small amount of gold was given to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

440
00:35:31,095 --> 00:35:36,795
So, the Messenger of Allah said: Where is the Persian man, where's your Persian brother?

441
00:35:37,495 --> 00:35:38,782
أين اَخَو كُمُ الْفَارِسِيْ

442
00:35:39,576 --> 00:35:41,319
So, they went and called Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي),

443
00:35:41,818 --> 00:35:45,196
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them take this gold and free yourself, with it.

444
00:35:45,831 --> 00:35:48,165
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: O Rasool Allah, what would this do?

445
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:55,805
When Salman(سلمان) saw the amount of gold, it appeared to be very small and wouldn't be sufficient.

446
00:35:56,345 --> 00:35:59,506
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them take it and it will be enough.

447
00:36:00,031 --> 00:36:04,435
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: I took it and it was weighed and it came out 40 ounces exactly.

448
00:36:06,051 --> 00:36:11,154
He said and then I was free and I never missed anything with Rasool Allah ﷺ after that,

449
00:36:11,234 --> 00:36:13,414
and the first battle he participated in, was.?

450
00:36:14,067 --> 00:36:14,900
Al-Khandaq(الخندق).

451
00:36:15,837 --> 00:36:17,873
And we all know his participation in it.

452
00:36:17,993 --> 00:36:22,359
He was the one, who came up with the idea of the trench.

453
00:36:23,376 --> 00:36:28,076
So, that is the story of Salman Al-Farsi رضي الله عنه

454
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,984
A few notes on his story,

455
00:36:33,705 --> 00:36:39,836
Who is the first man Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) ended up studying with?

456
00:36:40,946 --> 00:36:42,948
He was the bishop in Syria,

457
00:36:43,667 --> 00:36:45,664
What does Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) say about him?

458
00:36:46,192 --> 00:36:53,440
He said: So I joined him, but he was an evil man, demanding alms from his people,

459
00:36:53,893 --> 00:36:59,621
and whatever they collected, he would store away for himself and not give to the poor.

460
00:37:00,058 --> 00:37:03,754
Eventually, he had gathered seven jars of gold and silver,

461
00:37:04,483 --> 00:37:08,372
I hated him mightily for what I saw him doing.

462
00:37:09,433 --> 00:37:13,153
So, here we have somebody who's in search of the truth

463
00:37:13,991 --> 00:37:25,531
and he ends up meeting a person who has all the qualifications of turning him away of making him give up.

464
00:37:26,382 --> 00:37:30,195
But the zeal that Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) had was stronger than that.

465
00:37:31,121 --> 00:37:37,433
Nowadays, we say that sometimes our actions as Muslims is what causes the people to turn away from Islam.

466
00:37:38,650 --> 00:37:40,739
Well, that is true to a certain extent.

467
00:37:40,819 --> 00:37:45,531
But if somebody is sincere in their search of finding the truth,

468
00:37:46,399 --> 00:37:51,969
they should realize and understand that the truth is something and what the people are doing is something else.

469
00:37:52,463 --> 00:37:57,045
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) did not reject Christianity because the man he met was such a corrupt person.

470
00:37:57,897 --> 00:38:00,675
He stuck with him and he remained

471
00:38:01,081 --> 00:38:04,638
and then Allah سبحانه وتعالى rewarded him for that later on.

472
00:38:05,046 --> 00:38:08,446
He ended up being with the best man that he has ever seen.

473
00:38:08,486 --> 00:38:10,587
And in the description of that man, what did he say?

474
00:38:11,390 --> 00:38:14,657
He said, then they brought another man to take his place

475
00:38:14,862 --> 00:38:20,282
and I never saw a man, who did not attend the five prayers, who was better than he,

476
00:38:20,847 --> 00:38:24,557
What Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) means by a man who did not attend the five daily prayers is, that

477
00:38:24,952 --> 00:38:29,917
this is the best man I have ever seen before meeting the Muslims, before the followers of Muhammadﷺ

478
00:38:29,957 --> 00:38:31,873
because they are the ones who pray five times a day.

479
00:38:32,108 --> 00:38:36,552
So, he said the best person I met the most righteous and pious person I met

480
00:38:36,984 --> 00:38:40,132
before I met the Sahabah(صحابہ) of Rasool Allah ﷺ was this man,

481
00:38:40,842 --> 00:38:43,609
Allah rewarded him for his Sabr(صبر) and patience.

482
00:38:43,897 --> 00:38:45,248
And we learned two things from this.

483
00:38:45,288 --> 00:38:46,145
Number one

484
00:38:47,407 --> 00:38:48,812
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says:

485
00:38:49,256 --> 00:38:55,991
وَالَّذِينَ اهْتَدَوْا زَادَهُمْ هُدًى وَآتَاهُمْ تَقْوَاهُمْ۝

486
00:38:56,157 --> 00:39:00,369
The ones, who search for guidance, Allah will give it to them, but you have to look for it,

487
00:39:01,037 --> 00:39:02,509
you have to put in some effort.

488
00:39:03,221 --> 00:39:07,906
And when you do the reward that you get is more than what you put in.

489
00:39:08,487 --> 00:39:11,382
If you walk towards Allah, Allah will run towards you.

490
00:39:11,844 --> 00:39:15,184
If you take one step towards Allah, Allah will take many steps towards you

491
00:39:15,427 --> 00:39:18,242
but you have to take that first step, you have to take it.

492
00:39:19,131 --> 00:39:21,494
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) was searching for it and he got it.

493
00:39:21,945 --> 00:39:28,176
Allah سبحانه وتعالى ended up guiding him even though he belonged to a land that was hundreds of miles away,

494
00:39:28,799 --> 00:39:32,997
but he ended up receiving the truth because of his sincerity.

495
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:41,325
Number two, we shouldn't be turned off or let down, when we see somebody who's not doing the right thing.

496
00:39:42,129 --> 00:39:45,633
That is something that has nothing to do with the message itself.

497
00:39:46,652 --> 00:39:53,741
And Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي), he realized that and he remained with the man until he died and then he ended up being with a better person.

498
00:39:54,996 --> 00:40:07,265
The second note is that there were remnants of true believers before the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

499
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:12,555
but they were dying, and they were not leaving anyone behind them.

500
00:40:13,163 --> 00:40:17,114
And that is why the world was thirsty for the message of Muhammadﷺ.

501
00:40:18,197 --> 00:40:28,440
The third lesson to learn is that the Muslim community must be supportive of its new members.

502
00:40:29,077 --> 00:40:33,647
Rasool Allah ﷺ helped Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي), free himself, from slavery.

503
00:40:34,227 --> 00:40:38,845
And he requested the Sahabah to pitch in and participate

504
00:40:39,613 --> 00:40:43,941
as Muslims living in the West, it will become a duty among us,

505
00:40:44,038 --> 00:40:50,503
to take care of the needs of the new comers to the religion

506
00:40:51,673 --> 00:40:55,501
And many times these needs will be financial.

507
00:40:57,034 --> 00:40:58,226
And they need to be helped

508
00:40:59,329 --> 00:41:01,023
and this is part of Da'wah(دعوة)

509
00:41:01,546 --> 00:41:06,094
because Da'wah(دعوة) is not that you throw out words which are free to give, it doesn't cost you anything.

510
00:41:07,061 --> 00:41:14,134
Da'wah(دعوة) is also that you have to be responsible for the people who will join in your ranks.

511
00:41:14,811 --> 00:41:21,713
And notice that many of the early Muslims were people who were in need Bilal رضي الله عنه was freed by Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

512
00:41:22,291 --> 00:41:25,961
Many of the early Muslims were slaves that were in need of a lot of financial help

513
00:41:26,461 --> 00:41:29,894
because they were thrown away by their masters.

514
00:41:30,066 --> 00:41:34,263
Or you would have for example someone like Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير), who came from a very wealthy family

515
00:41:34,828 --> 00:41:39,144
but his mother refused to give him anything after he became Muslim.

516
00:41:39,728 --> 00:41:43,855
So, these members are in need of support in their initial stages.

517
00:41:44,221 --> 00:41:48,668
And the risk is that if they don't get help in those critical stages, they could apostate,

518
00:41:49,444 --> 00:41:56,409
and there is a study that was done in America that found that quite a significant number of reverts end up leaving Islam.

519
00:41:57,235 --> 00:42:00,010
Quite a large number, I don't remember the exact figure,

520
00:42:00,231 --> 00:42:04,182
but a lot of them end up leaving Islam because of the difficulties that they face.

521
00:42:04,396 --> 00:42:08,479
First of all many of them are stripped, from their social belonging,

522
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:13,016
their social life, their families neglect them, their friends leave them,

523
00:42:13,429 --> 00:42:18,990
so they are in need of a social belonging they have to have a new Association.

524
00:42:19,829 --> 00:42:23,742
Number two, many of them come with some dire financial needs

525
00:42:24,366 --> 00:42:27,947
and if they don't get them you know a human being is a human being,

526
00:42:28,468 --> 00:42:30,609
if the belly is going empty,

527
00:42:31,115 --> 00:42:32,566
like I mentioned in the Hadith(حديث),

528
00:42:33,018 --> 00:42:36,179
بَازِرُوْ بِالْاَعْمَالِ سَبْعَه هَلْ تَنْتَظِرُوْنَ اِلَّا فَقْرًا مُنْسِيْهَ

529
00:42:36,813 --> 00:42:40,441
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Do the good deeds before seven things could happen.

530
00:42:40,673 --> 00:42:43,580
And one of them is Faqram Munsiyyah(فَقْرًا مُنْسِيْه) poverty that will make you forget,

531
00:42:44,019 --> 00:42:46,104
if your stomach is empty, you will forget everything.

532
00:42:47,434 --> 00:42:49,327
A person who is going around hungry,

533
00:42:49,649 --> 00:42:53,686
cannot think about spirituality and learning Ilm(علم) and knowledge,

534
00:42:54,082 --> 00:42:56,897
a person in that stage would want to feed their stomach.

535
00:42:57,710 --> 00:43:02,181
So, these are things that are part of our program of Da'wah(دعوة), we have to have institutions

536
00:43:02,817 --> 00:43:07,031
that would satisfy and fulfill the needs of the new Muslim.

537
00:43:07,775 --> 00:43:13,368
And that is part of our duty as Muslims living in non Muslim societies,

538
00:43:13,408 --> 00:43:16,800
where there are people who are embracing Islam.

539
00:43:18,515 --> 00:43:22,657
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

